      "display_order": 1,
      "question_text": "The variables $x$ and $y$ satisfy the differential equation\n\n$$\\cos 2x \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = \\frac{4 \\tan 2x}{\\sin^2 3y},$$\n\nwhere $0 \\le x < \\frac{1}{4}\\pi$. It is given that $y = 0$ when $x = \\frac{1}{6}\\pi$.\n\nSolve the differential equation to obtain the value of $x$ when $y = \\frac{1}{6}\\pi$. Give your answer correct to 3 decimal places.",
